  "title": "BigP3BCI Study K — 9x8 adaptive/checkerboard, 2 sessions (5 healthy subjects)",
  "description": "A subset (Study K) of the bigP3BCI collection, a large public P300-based brain-computer interface speller dataset. It contains 16-channel EEG recorded with a g.USBamp at 256 Hz from 5 healthy participants across 2 sessions. Participants used a 9x8 character grid with adaptive and checkerboard stimulus presentation, and target and non-target events are annotated with HED tags.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 16 channels (standard 10-20 montage) with a g.tec g.USBamp at 256 Hz in a laboratory setting. Participants performed a P300 speller task on a 9x8 grid with online feedback, using a calibration-then-test scheme. Target and NonTarget events were epoched over 0-1.0 s.",
